Yes. Looking at the latest `SignViewer`, I would change the **YouTube implementation itself**. The current approach creates an `<iframe>` manually and then asks `YT.Player` to attach to that iframe. That can be unreliable when React is repeatedly mounting/unmounting the player during the sequence. Your current YouTube rendering is at lines 320–331. 

The most reliable approach is:

**React renders an empty `<div>` → YouTube API creates the iframe inside it.**

That also makes the MP4 → YouTube → MP4 transitions much cleaner.

