### One thing to check

If **a particular YouTube video still doesn't load** after this change, look at the browser console. The `onError` now prints the YouTube error code and video ID. Common causes are that the video owner has **disabled embedding**, the video is unavailable/restricted, or the ID being passed is wrong. That's different from the sequence bug.

The main change I recommend right now is **switching from manually rendering `<iframe>` + `YT.Player(iframe)` to letting `YT.Player` create the iframe inside a `<div>`**. Your current implementation mixes those two approaches.
